    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate prioritizing high-ceiling matchups against weak pitching, with **Corbin Carroll** standing as our undisputed anchor. His 87.14 score is bolstered by a prime matchup against Ryan Feltner (4.96 xERA) and an aggressive placement in the #2 hole, making him a high-efficiency engine for Runs and, crucially, our most reliable source for the scarce Stolen Base category. **Mickey Moniak** (75.75) and **Gabriel Moreno** (71.10) also project as elite starts against suspect pitching; **Mickey Moniak** specifically benefits from a massive 14% platoon boost against Merrill Kelly, while **Gabriel Moreno** gains significant efficiency from both the favorable SP xERA and his projected #3 spot in the order. \n\nThe optimizer leaned heavily into park-adjusted splits and order placement, which created a difficult decision for the final utility spots. **Max Muncy** (42.29) was the most difficult exclusion from the starting lineup, pushed to the bench only because the aggressive efficiency of **Josh Naylor** (62.07) and the high-leverage utility of our infielders provided a safer floor against the day's pitching slate. While **Zach McKinstry** (47.30) carries a marginal score, he remains in the lineup specifically for his ability to target the stolen base scarcity; his 100% SB potential against the slow delivery of Foster Griffin offers a specialized utility that justifies the start despite his low base projection.\n\nWe remain cautious regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status of several key starters, including **Gabriel Moreno**, **Isaac Paredes**, and **Brice Turang**. While our projections account for historical averages, any late-scratch or order adjustments could significantly impact the 5x5 Roto efficiency. Additionally, while **Tyler Soderstrom** draws a highly favorable park boost, he faces the toughest arm of our core\u2014Drew Rasmussen (3.17 xERA)\u2014limiting his ceiling to 57.87. We continue to monitor the status of **James Wood**, who remains on the IL, as we look to stabilize our roster depth in the coming days alongside stashed assets like **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, and **Trevor Story**.",
